{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"glad-monotonous-greatargus","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\nA plan-review run on current `main` emitted, from `rebar.llm.plan_review.workflow_ops`:\n\n    plan-review Pass-2 verification contract violation ... {'unexpected': [0, 1, 2, 3]}\n\nEVERY verification index was rejected as unexpected, so all four findings degraded to\nINDETERMINATE. Observed during a real `review-plan` run at HEAD `1052bc856f`, not in a test.\n\n## Why this matters more than the verdict suggests\n\nThe run's VERDICT was unchanged, which is exactly what makes this dangerous: Pass-2 is the\nverification pass that decides whether a Pass-1 finding is real. If every index is rejected, the\ngate is not verifying anything — it is degrading the whole set to INDETERMINATE and continuing.\nA reviewer reading only PASS/BLOCK sees a healthy gate.\n\nConsequences to establish in the investigation:\n* Does an INDETERMINATE finding still count toward the blocking decision, or is it silently\n  dropped? If dropped, a run in this state cannot BLOCK on a Pass-2-verified criterion at all.\n* How long has this been live? Every plan review taken as authoritative while it persists is\n  suspect, including several signed during this epic.\n\n## What is known\n\n* Reproduced at HEAD `1052bc856f` (plain `origin/main`, not the provider-seam stack).\n* The rejected index set was `[0, 1, 2, 3]` — a contiguous run from zero, i.e. ALL of them, which\n  points at an index-BASIS mismatch (chunk-local vs global numbering, or a re-chunk between\n  request and response) rather than at individual bad indices.\n* The emitting site is in `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py`; the verify kernel that\n  assigns the global `index` is `src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py`.\n\n## Approach\n\nInvestigate with /rebar-debug discipline: capture the ACTUAL request and response at the Pass-2\nboundary — the indices sent and the indices returned — rather than reasoning from the code. Choose\nthe capture point one layer BELOW the contract check, since the check only reports the mismatch and\ncannot show which side is wrong.\n\nDo NOT assume the model returned bad data. An index-basis mismatch on rebar's side produces exactly\nthis signature, and the contiguous-from-zero set is more consistent with a basis error than with a\nmodel fault.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- AC1: The root cause is proven by a captured request/response pair at the Pass-2 boundary showing\n  which side's indices are wrong, not by code reading alone.\n- AC2: A regression test reproduces the mismatch and fails before the fix.\n- AC3: After the fix, a real plan-review run emits no contract violation and findings retain their\n  verified severity rather than degrading to INDETERMINATE.\n- AC4: It is stated explicitly whether INDETERMINATE findings can block, and if they cannot, whether\n  any gate decision made while this was live needs revisiting.\n- AC5: make lint and make typecheck pass by exit code; the default selection is green.","id":"d5c7-0d57-c3ab-4e93","parent_id":"061c-ecd1-8967-4a76","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Plan-review Pass-2 rejects every verification index and degrades all findings to INDETERMINATE, live on main"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785688567732250001,"uuid":"86d25234-7ead-4fbe-ab57-a0163ae7b198"}